        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"BlueHairedMeerkat\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluehairedmeerkat/48/1967_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> BlueHairedMeerkat:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>TakeWalker wrote:</b><br><blockquote>You don't have to hate Twitch to not have the time/forget a stream is happening! I prefer Youtube because I can watch those at my leisure.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nNo, but I beleive the 'What do you have against Twitch?' comment was aimed at the 'I truly detest Twitch' above it.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Exactly. They end up on YouTube anyways - and you can watch past Twitch broadcasts too (for a certain length of time), unless for some reason they don't have the option enabled to save them. Even if they don't, they can make highlights and save them on Twitch indefinitely.</p>\n<p>I've watched a couple \"live streaming to YouTube\" things and the interaction is just terrible. There's no chat (or it just wasn't working) so we had to just post comments and hope they saw them. Twitch with a live chat is so much better.</p>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
